## Failure Mode Taxonomy (38/63 Baseline)

Analysing the 25 wrong answers in the best local run:

| Category | Count | Description |
|---|---|---|
| SymPy TypeError | 5 | `TypeError: Cannot convert expression to float` — model calls `float(N(expr))` on a symbolic expression that still contains variable `x` |
| Wrong code logic | 5 | Code runs without error but computes the wrong quantity (wrong formula, wrong approach) |
| Conceptual/stats error | 8 | Stats methodology questions (Hawthorne effect, selection bias, response variable, t-test assumptions) where model picks wrong option |
| Code crashes | 4 | Other runtime errors (CoercionFailed, NameError, TypeError) |
| Abstract algebra logic | 3 | Z_3 irreducibility, coset structure — correct setup but domain/modular arithmetic implementation fails |

The most impactful remaining improvement opportunity is the `TypeError: Cannot convert expression to float` category, which affects questions where the model correctly identifies the approach but `float(N(expr))` is applied to an expression with free variables (e.g., `x+11` instead of a number).

